Core Innovations & Contributions / 核心创新与贡献
•	The 12-Core OS Chips: Built to adapt to contemporary technological conditions, integrating the strengths of historical public power operating systems into a foundational framework for sovereign citizen control over public power.

•	12核心OS芯片晶片拓扑：创造构建了适应当时技术条件，集大成人类公权力运行制度的优点，具有即时可操作性的，主权民众对公权力掌控的基石。

•	Low-Barrier Public Office Access: Creates the lowest threshold and broadest direct public office equity system, shifting elections from choosing others to choosing oneself, minimizing rent-seeking space and reducing constitutional crises.

•	公职平权体系：创造了最低的门槛，最广泛直接的公职平权体系，实现了选举由选他人向选自己的方向转变，从技术层面最大程度的限制权力寻租空间。

•	24/7 AI Oversight: Transitions from selecting traditional leaders to choosing competent public power executors, utilizing AI for 24-hour sovereign reverse oversight of government.

•	AI逆向监督政府：把传统的选举领导人，向选择有能力的公权力执行者的目标转变，把AI用于主权反向监督政府──日常24小时全时全量监督公权力的执行者。

•	Civilian Jury & Quantum Finality: Selecting grassroots AI algorithms via citizen jury forms—quantum flicker one-click finality, leaving capital with no physical targets.

•	平民陪审员与量子闪烁：参照平民陪审员形式选最底层的AI算法──量子闪烁一键定音/资本找不到任何肉体靶子。

•	Open Source Algorithms & Merit Reports: Open algorithms make ideas the most legitimate hard-core capital for re-election. Departing or contesting officials must submit a report on necessity, duties, and improvement proposals.

•	开源算法来源：机制公开让思想成为连任最合法的硬核资本，特定职位官员离职或者参与竞选特定职位，必须制作改进报告。

2. Convention Articles / 公约条款正文
Article 1: Equal Access and Intellectual Exoskeleton / 第一条：平民公职准入平权与主权智力赋能
•	Equal Access: Contracting parties shall gradually abolish unreasonable barriers based on property, origin, social class, political faction, or non-performance factors.

•	公职准入资格平权：缔约各方应逐步废除以财产、出身、社会阶层、政治派系及非履职能力因素为依据的不合理公职竞选门槛。

•	Intellectual Exoskeleton: Provide AGI and advanced AI computing, knowledge bases, and analysis tools equally and free of charge to all registered citizens.

•	智力外骨骼赋能：缔约各方应通过公约开放网关，向所有依法登记参选的公民免费、平等地提供通用人工智能（AGI）及其他先进人工智能系统的算力与决策辅助服务。

Article 2: AI Reverse Oversight and Power Fuse / 第二条：AI 逆向监督与公职权力熔断
•	Computing Limits: Prohibit using AGI computing power for unjustified generalized surveillance of ordinary citizens.

•	算力用途限制：缔约各方应禁止将通用人工智能算力用于缺乏合法依据的对普通公民普遍性监控。

•	59-Score Warning & Fuse: Establish a quantitative evaluation system (Q-value). A score below 59 triggers a red-card warning, independent review, and potential smart contract freezing of administrative signing rights.

•	59分公职风险预警与熔断：建立公职履职量化评估体系（Q 值），Q 值低于五十九（59）分时，系统应立即发出红牌预警，底层智能合约可以秒级冻结该公职人员之行政签署权与决策权。

Article 3: Civilian Jury and Cognitive Voting Network / 第三条：平民评审团与认知投票网络
•	Sovereign Protection Jury: Establish a sovereign protection jury composed of ordinary citizens and professionals, generated through auditable random selection procedures.

•	主权护民评审团：建立由普通公民与相关领域专业人员共同参与的主权护民评审团，成员应通过依法授权、可审计的随机抽选程序产生。

•	Privacy & Verifiable Voting: Utilize Zero-Knowledge Proofs (ZKP), anonymous credentials, and encrypted tallying to protect voter identity while ensuring verifiable results.

•	隐私保护与可验证投票：选举及陪评投票系统应采用零知识证明（ZKP）、匿名凭证、加密计票及其他适当技术，保护选民身份与选择秘密，并确保投票结果可独立验证。

Article 4: Digital Trust and Crisis Simulation / 第四条：公职智库数字信托与危机仿真考核
•	Governance Algorithm Openness: Establish a distributed public office think-tank digital trust network, publicly releasing governance algorithms and policy evaluation models via GitHub.

•	治理算法开放：建立分布式公职智库数字信托网络，依法公开可公开的国家治理算法、政策评估模型，并通过 GitHub 等开放平台征集全球研究人员、技术开发者及公众提出的改进方案。

•	Blind Testing: Candidates and policies undergo blind testing in reproducible, auditable simulation environments.

•	盲测验证与履职资格：候选人及其政策方案应在预先设定、可复现、可审计的仿真环境中接受盲测，并通过对抗测试、极端情境测试及长期影响评估。

Article 5: De-identified Screening and Cross-Debates / 第五条：去身份化初筛与高强度交叉辩论
•	Anonymous Screening: Hide names, portraits, voices, genders, and political affiliations during the primary screening stage to focus on policy execution results.

•	匿名化初筛：公职选举初筛阶段，应在可行范围内隐藏候选人的姓名、肖像、声音、性别及政治派系等与履职能力无直接关联的身份信息。

•	High-Intensity Cross-Debates: Advancing candidates participate in randomized topic cross-debates and emergency crisis simulations under uniform rules.

•	高强度交叉辩论：晋级候选人应参加随机抽题交叉辩论、突发危机仿真、跨领域政策协调及利益冲突处置等程序，在相同规则和信息条件下接受检验。

Article 6: Shadow Cabinet and Avatar Shield / 第六条：影子内阁精算与虚拟分身隔离公投
•	Shadow Cabinet Simulation: Organize multiple shadow cabinet groups to simulate resource allocation, policy coordination, and crisis response among departments.

•	影子内阁仿真：对初筛后入围的候选人，可组织多组影子内阁，模拟政府部门之间的资源配置、政策协调、利益冲突与危机应对。

•	Avatar Shield Isolation: Utilize neutral virtual avatars to replace candidates' real appearances during final evaluations, reducing bias from appearance, voice, and media packaging.

•	虚拟分身隔离：在最终评议阶段，可采用“Avatar Shield”数字分身隔离程序，以统一的中性虚拟形象代替候选人的真实面貌，降低外貌、声音、名望及媒体包装对评议结果的影响。

Article 7: Term Limits and Rotation / 第七条：公职任期交错轮换与权力连续性保障
•	Maximum Term Length: Set cumulative service limits for national and state executive heads (e.g., maximum of six years) to prevent power solidification.

•	最高履职年限：缔约各方应建立公职任期及累计履职年限限制制度。国家及州级行政长官的累计履职年限可设定为最高六（6）年。

•	Staggered Rotation Mechanism: Establish dual-track positions, staggered elections, and batch replacement mechanisms to avoid changing all positions simultaneously.

•	交错轮换机制：缔约各方应根据行政职位类别、法定任期及权力结构，建立双轨职位、交错选举与分批更替机制，避免全部职位在同一时间集中更替。

Article 8: Dual-Track Nomination / 第八条：技术公职 AI 提名与行政首脑自主任命双轨制
•	Executive Core Appointments: Legally produced executive heads maintain direct appointment rights over core staff and advisors to ensure policy coordination and political responsibility.

•	行政首脑核心团队任命权：经合法程序产生的行政首脑，应依法享有对其部分核心幕僚及政策顾问团队的直接任命权，以保障行政决策的协调性与政治责任的明确性。

•	AI-Assisted Technical Nominations: Use AI-assisted talent selection based on public qualifications and merit tests to recommend top candidates for technical public offices.

•	技术类公职和另外一部分核心幕僚及政策顾问团队的AI 辅助提名：对技术类公职和另外部分核心幕僚及政策顾问团队采用AI 辅助提名，推荐综合评价排名靠前的候选人供法定机关审议。

Article 9: Lifecycle Equality Wallet and Incentives / 第九条：全生命周期平权钱包与参选激励制度
•	Sovereign Cognitive Incentives: Citizens receive incentive funds upon completing legally prescribed electoral procedures or governance practices, lowering economic barriers.

•	主权认知参选激励：公民完成依法规定的参选程序或符合条件的公共治理实践后，可依照统一、透明的规则获得主权认知参选激励金，降低公民参与公共事务的经济门槛。

•	Lifelong Support Accounts: Establish supportive accounts from birth, providing phased education, public affairs study, and mock election incentives.

•	托举钱包与成长支持：缔约各方可为公民建立自出生起依法登记、分阶段管理的托举账户，并根据年龄与法律能力提供相应的教育、公共事务学习及模拟竞选激励。

Article 10: Public Election Funds and Enterprise Contribution / 第十条：公共选举基金与企业贡献公平机制
•	Publicization of Political Funds: Establish independent, public, and auditable public election funds, restricting private political donations to political figures.

•	政治资金公共化：缔约各方应建立独立、公开、可审计的公共选举基金，依法限制向政治人物及其关联组织提供私人政治献金。

•	Comprehensive Corporate Contributions: Evaluate enterprises based on financial feedback, labor relations, resource/energy efficiency, and long-term credit.

•	企业公共贡献综合评价：建立企业公共贡献评价机制，从财务反哺、劳资关系、资源与能源利用效率、长期信用及其他可核验指标等方面综合评估企业的公共责任表现。

Article 11: Global Peace Defense and War Decision-Making / 第十一条：全球和平防御机制与战争决策权力分流
•	Peace Defense Early Warning: Establish global peace defense early warning algorithms to prevent, suspend, and eliminate the root causes of war using joint forces.

•	和平防御预警与资产保护：缔约各方均应设立全球和平防御预警算法，以全部缔约各方的共同力量，避免和中止和消灭产生战争的根源。

•	Strategic and Tactical Separation: Separate political authorization and strategic command from tactical military execution, ensuring civilian leadership retains supervision and accountability rights.

•	战略授权与战术指挥分离：战争与军事行动的政治授权、战略目标、法律边界及军事战术指挥重新进行明确分工。文职领导人不代替军方做具体军事行动决策，但统帅、监督及终止授权等权力不得被技术系统取消。

3. Conclusion / 结语
•	English: Do not mistake the description in this text for reality. When we look up and see strategic bombers carrying immense wealth and cutting-edge technology flying overhead, we must ask: Can these forces created by humanity be invoked? Why cannot they be used first to safeguard life and maintain peace?
When we see political figures making commitments on behalf of the public in the media, we must ask: Why do they represent us? Why do people follow them? By whom are their actions supervised, and by whom are their commitments verified?
When enterprises and capital face public procurement, policy changes, and market competition while individuals get rich through power and influence, we must ask: How can we truly lock power inside a cage?
These questions point to the same place: Public power affects the destiny of everyone, but how can the public truly participate in the generation, operation, supervision, and error-correction of public power?
How can peace be more than a wish, how can power be supervised, and how can institutional safeguards allow more people to participate equally in shaping humanity's common future?
Digital technology and artificial intelligence offer new possibilities to answer this question, but the intervention of AI in the operation of public power also generates new risks. This is the question raised in this text, and it is a problem that requires everyone to participate in solving together. Humanity's capacity to create wealth and master technology continues to grow, but the speed at which institutions adapt to technology lags far behind. Problems such as unequal opportunities for public participation, insufficient power supervision, information asymmetry, and international conflicts still persist.
A common future is jointly created by humanity. May everyone have more equal opportunities for public participation, enable public offices to bear responsibilities better matched to their power, subject major public decisions to digital supervision, and allow the capabilities created by science, technology, and capital to better serve the common security, dignity, and prosperity of humanity.
Mass Humans MoreUp !!
•	中文： 不要被本文的描述当现实，当我们抬头看到凝聚巨大财富与顶尖科技的战略轰炸机从头顶飞过，我们要追问：这些人类创造的力量，是可以调用的？为什么不能首先用于守护生命与维护和平？
当我们在媒体上看到政治人物代表公众作出承诺，我们要追问：他们为什么要代表我们？为什么有人追随他们？他们的行为由谁监督，承诺由谁检验？
当企业与资本面对公共采购、政策变化和市场竞争，而个别人靠权势发财时，我们要问：如何真正把权力锁进笼子里？
这些问题指向同一个地方：公共权力影响这每个人的命运，但公众如何才能真正参与公权力的产生、运行、监督与纠错？
如何让和平不止于愿望，让权力能够被监督，让制度保障让更多人平等参与塑造人类的共同未来？
数字技术与人工智能为回答这一问题提供了新的可能，但人工智能介入共权力运行也会产生新的风险。这是本文提出的问题，也是需要大家共同参与，一起来解决的问题。人类创造财富与掌握技术的能力不断增强，但制度适应技术的速度远远落后。公共参与机会不均、权力监督不足、信息不对称和国际冲突等问题仍然存在。
共同未来，人类共同创造。愿每一个人都拥有更平等的公共参与机会，让公共职位承担与其权力更为匹配的责任，让重大公共决策受到数字化监督，让科技与资本创造的能力更多服务于人类共同的安全、尊严与繁荣。

